Bootstrap-size observation
--------------------------

The first linked Qwen task starts at offset `0x0`.
Its `NextPointer` is `0x200`, but the converted header uses `td_size=0x274`.
The KMD programs `TQ_SIZE1` from `td_size`, so the current bootstrap fetch
extends `0x74` bytes into the next task.

The probe now accepts a hexadecimal `--td-size` override. This allows a
clean-boot test of the first task with `--td-count 1 --td-size 0x200`.

Red test:

  AttributeError: module 'production_anec_probe' has no attribute 'parse_int'

Green command:

  uv run --with numpy python -m unittest tools.test_hwxv2_to_anec tools.test_production_anec_probe && uv run ruff check tools/production-anec-probe.py tools/test_production_anec_probe.py

Observed output:

